        "original_id": "aeed3e10-7897-580a-80a4-b17587781fd2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Henke, Russell Humphreys\n- Projects: RATE project\n- Organizations: Creation Research Society, Institute for Creation Research\n- Concepts: radiometric dating, dating techniques, recent creation, zircons, helium, young-earth creationism\n\nFacts:\n- The RATE project, short for Radioisotopes and the Age of The Earth, was conducted by the Creation Research Society and the Institute for Creation Research from 1997 to 2005.\n- The RATE project assessed the validity of radiometric dating and other dating techniques in light of the doctrine of a recent creation.\n- The RATE project claimed that zircons contain too much helium to be billions of years old.\n- Kevin Henke has been critical of the RATE project's results.\n- Russell Humphreys was involved in the RATE project and is a young-earth creationist.\n- Kevin Henke argued that Russell Humphreys made errors in his research.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
